; naama-pratibodha: pronoun cross-reference — the recognition of a name through its proxy.
; a pronoun (its, their, it) does not name directly; it awakens (pratibodha) the name.
; antisymmetric: pronoun refers to entity, not entity refers to pronoun.
; NOT transitive: reference does not chain.
; example: [its, naama-pratibodha, ball]  from "find its kinetic energy"
; 
; naama       = name (the thing being pointed at)
; pratibodha  = awakening / recognition (the act of knowing which name is meant)

(sangati naama-pratibodha
  (sthita vak-sthalam sambandha directed-graph)
  (abheda naama-mudra))
